cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this addon, cite godot-sandbox.
title: godot-sandbox (Godot addon, vendored binaries)
abstract: >-
  The godot_sandbox addon: the Sandbox node that runs RISC-V guest ELFs under
  libriscv inside stock Godot, the only native code the loop needs. Vendored
  as prebuilt GDExtension libraries with the addon's scripts and icons
  (Gate 0E, commit bb149bf of this repo). The Linux x86_64 library was
  replaced on 2026-09-23 with the build of V-Sekai-fire/godot-sandbox at
  a45da9f (main after PR #4, whose Sandbox::handle_exception starts the C++
  Docker container only when sandbox/toolchain/docker_enabled is true;
  project.godot sets it false), taken from that repository's Actions run
  35876410662 (the PR build, tree identical to a45da9f), artifact
  godot-sandbox-linux-x86_64-single, sha256
  fdf85871b6a93f161000cf66bfd84db683ac3c6137ad9760e0961fc7f8d3ea8e. It is
  what the RunPod loop worker loads (Gate 0H). Replaced again on 2026-09-24
  with a build of V-Sekai-fire/godot-sandbox b1118e5 (main, 2026-09-23) plus
  the one commit of branch feat/bintr-emit
  (tools/godot-sandbox/0001-bintr-emit.patch: GODOT_SANDBOX_BINTR_EMIT=<dir>
  writes each program's native translation as C99), built with Ubuntu clang
  18, CMake and Ninja, Release, RISCV_ASMJIT=OFF (no JIT; binary translation
  lookup as before), sha256
  711e7a1363a9fb5b12ebe4ef031564635acf9fab6064b48787ec416abe348648. The Windows libraries are the
  ones vendored at Gate 0E; their source commit was not recorded then.
authors:
  - name: Alf-André Walla (fwsGonzo)
